  "text": "Radiation Oncology in Yonkers | Animal Specialty Center\nSkip to Primary Content\nBook\nContact Us\nMap\n9 Odell Plaza,\nYonkers,\nNY,\n10701\nCall\n(914) 457-4000\nEmergency\nEmergency\nPhone:\n(914) 457-4000\nAddress:\n9 Odell Plaza,\nYonkers,\nNY,\n10701\nOur Team\nServices\nCardiology\nDermatology\nEmergency\nInternal Medicine\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nRadiation Oncology\nSurgery\nPet Owners\nReferring Veterinarians\nCareer Growth\nEmergency\nContact Us\nRadiation\nOncology\nCancer Care Options for Your Pet at Animal Specialty Center\nAt Animal Specialty Center, we understand how difficult a cancer diagnosis for your pet can be. Our compassionate radiation oncology team is here to support you and your pet every step of the way. If you have been referred to our hospital or would like to schedule a consultation with one of our radiation oncologists, call us to make an appointment.\nContact Us\nWhat is Veterinary Radiation Oncology?\nVeterinary Radiation Oncology is a specialized type of cancer treatment that involves radiation therapy to help control internal and external cancerous masses or tumors. Masses or tumors that have been unresponsive to other procedures or that cannot be surgically removed can also respond well to radiation therapy. Radiation therapy is often used in conjunction with surgery, chemotherapy, and other treatment methods.\nRadiation Therapy Treatments\nRadiation therapy is delivered to the location of the cancerous tumor or mass with a linear accelerator.  At Animal Specialty Center, we use a Varian TrueBeam with a sophisticated radiotherapy planning system that enables our veterinary care team to treat a broad range of cancer cases.  Our machine is designed with exceptional speed and accuracy, which ensures comprehensive and effective care.\nTypes of Radiation Therapy\nConventional Radiation Therapy (CRT) / Intensity Modulated Radiation Therapy (IMRT)\nDelivers multiple small doses over time for long-term tumor control.\nTypically used for mast cell tumors (16 treatments).\nModerate-to-marked temporary side effects expected, peaking a few weeks after treatment.\nStereotactic Radiation Therapy (SRT/SRS/SBRT)\nHigh-dose, highly focused radiation delivered in 1, 3, or 5 sessions.\nRequires a CT scan for precise targeting.\nFewer hospital visits and milder side effects compared to CRT.\nPalliative Radiation Therapy (PRT)\nMedium-dose radiation spaced over time to relieve pain and slow tumor growth.\nOften used for oral tumors in pets.\nEffects last 3–6 months; repeat treatments may be needed.\nElectron Therapy\nUsed for microscopic disease or surgical scars.\nRequires healed surgical sites; sometimes a CT scan is needed.\nUsually consists of 15–20 treatments.\nOur Radiation Oncology Team\nThe Veterinary Radiation Oncologists at Animal Specialty Center are here for you and your pet. We understand how overwhelming this process can be. Your pet is in good hands with our caring cancer care team. Learn more about our veterinary radiation oncologists below.\nKari Rosen\nDVM, DACVR, Medical Director\nRadiation Oncology\nView Profile\nKari Rosen\nDVM, DACVR, Medical Director\nRadiation Oncology\nView Profile\nAnimal Specialty Center\n9 Odell Plaza\nYonkers\n,\nNY\n10701\nT:\n(914) 457-4000\nF:\n(914) 457-4001\nHours of Operation\nMain Hours\nMon\nOpen 24 hrs\nTue\nOpen 24 hrs\nWed\nOpen 24 hrs\nThu\nOpen 24 hrs\nFri\nOpen 24 hrs\nSat\nOpen 24 hrs\nSun\nOpen 24 hrs\nContact Us\nOur Team\nCareer Growth\nPet Owners\nTerms & Conditions\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility\nCookie Preferences\nDo Not Sell or Share My Information\n©\nCopyright\n2026",
